  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Very warm to end the work week, then seasonal \nconditions for Halloween Weekend.\n\nA weak, dry cold front is progged to cross the region Friday \nmorning, possibly bringing some drizzle to the higher elevations of \nthe Alleghenies. High pressure builds into the region Friday \nafternoon through the weekend. Expect well above normal temperatures \nFriday as highs reach the mid to upper 70s. Would not be surprised \nif a spot or two in central VA reached 80F briefly. Some passing \nclouds are likely Friday morning to early afternoon, though the \nbackground environment is forecast to be very dry, so not expecting \nmuch impact on temperatures. Downsloping winds make for a breezy \nafternoon as winds gust around 20-25 mph, especially along/north of \nI-66/US-50. \n\nEventually, some cooler temperatures moves in Friday night through \nthe weekend. Expect seasonable and dry conditions as high pressure \nholds firm. A shortwave trough passing just south of the area on \nSunday won't amount to much as it lacks sufficient moisture or \nforcing to produce widespread shower activity.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Rain chances remain uncertain for the first half of \nnext week with a more appreciable chance during the latter half of \nnext week.\n\nHigh pressure should hold strong enough Sunday into Monday, where \nrain chances could be squashed or be confined to upslope rain \nshowers or sprinkles in the higher western elevations. As for \ntemperatures each day, they should be seasonable with highs in the \nlower to middle 60s.\n\nBy Tuesday into Wednesday, a strong trough of low pressure will \nbegin to push eastward from the Great Plains toward the Mississippi \nand Ohio Valleys. This will aid in weakening the high pressure over \nus. There are increasingly better rain chances ahead during this \nperiod. We may be waiting until Wednesday night and Thursday to see \nsome of these rain showers, but the chances are on the rise. \nTemperatures will become warmer as well Tuesday and Wednesday and \nreaching into the lower to middle 70s ahead of a strong trough from \nthe west.",
